      "source": [
        "## 4. Data cleaning and preprocessing\n",
        "\n",
        "- Remove duplicate rows.\n",
        "- Remove the customer ID from clustering because an ID is an identifier, not a measure of customer behaviour.\n",
        "- Convert columns to numeric when possible (including columns whose names contain `#` or `?`).\n",
        "- Fill missing numeric values with the median.\n",
        "- Cap extreme values using the IQR rule to reduce the influence of very large values. This is a practical preprocessing choice; it may also reduce genuine differences between high-value customers, so we compare results as exploratory segments.\n",
        "- Scale features because clustering depends on distances and the features have different units.\n",
        "\n",
        "The original dataset is kept in `df` so we can interpret clusters later."
      ]
    },
