      "source": [
        "## 8. DBSCAN clustering\n",
        "\n",
        "DBSCAN groups points that have enough nearby neighbours. It does not require us to choose the number of clusters in advance. Points that do not belong to a sufficiently dense region are labelled `-1` (noise).\n",
        "\n",
        "- `eps`: neighbourhood radius.\n",
        "- `min_samples`: minimum number of points needed to form a dense region.\n",
        "\n",
        "DBSCAN is sensitive to these settings and to feature scaling, so we explore more than one `eps` value."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 17,
      "id": "a38cce0c",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 501
        },
        "id": "a38cce0c",
        "outputId": "4a6a7b70-827b-4ab2-e7bc-3b4d9c18e8a6"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 800x500 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# A k-distance plot can help select a useful eps range.\n",
        "# We use min_samples=5 as a starting point.\n",
        "min_samples_value = 5\n",
        "neighbors = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min_samples_value)\n",
        "neighbors_fit = neighbors.fit(X_scaled)\n",
        "distances, indices = neighbors_fit.kneighbors(X_scaled)\n",
        "k_distances = np.sort(distances[:, -1])\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
        "plt.plot(k_distances)\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Points sorted by distance\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(f\"Distance to {min_samples_value}th nearest neighbour\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"DBSCAN k-Distance Plot\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "5fc662fe",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5fc662fe"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 8.1 Try different DBSCAN parameters\n",
        "\n",
        "We test several epsilon values. If the dataset is large, silhouette calculations use a sample to keep the notebook responsive. Noise points (`-1`) are excluded from the silhouette calculation because they are not a normal cluster."
      ]
