      "source": [
        "## 9. Compare the algorithms\n",
        "\n",
        "Silhouette score ranges from -1 to 1. Higher values generally indicate better-defined clusters. A score near 0 can mean clusters overlap; a negative score can mean points may be assigned to the wrong cluster.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Caution:** K-Means uses the full dataset, hierarchical clustering uses a sample, and DBSCAN may label some points as noise. Their scores are useful comparisons, but not perfectly identical experiments."
      ]
    },
